Code-embedding model — crates/argot-rules-semantic/model/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  embeddings.safetensors   int8 token-embedding table, 61,053 x 256
  tokenizer.json           byte-level BPE tokenizer, 61,053 entries

  Distilled from jina-embeddings-v2-base-code
    https://huggingface.co/jinaai/jina-embeddings-v2-base-code
    Copyright (c) Jina AI GmbH
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  The table was produced by running that model over its own vocabulary and
  reducing the result; the tokenizer is that model's, carried over unchanged.
  Both files are therefore derived from Apache-2.0 licensed work and are
  redistributed under that license. The files carry the same provenance in
  their safetensors `__metadata__`.

  The upstream model repository ships no NOTICE file (checked 2026-07-29),
  so Apache-2.0 section 4(d) has no upstream notice text to reproduce here.
  Whether Apache-2.0 attaches to model weights at all is unsettled; this
  NOTICE assumes it does, because the compliance cost is one file.

  Distilled with the model2vec technique
    https://github.com/MinishLab/model2vec
    Copyright (c) MinishLab
    Licensed under the MIT License

  The inference that reads these weights
  (crates/argot-rules-semantic/src/static_embedder.rs) is argot's own.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
BPE tokenizer — crates/argot-lang/data/unixcoder_tokenizer.json
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The serialised fast tokenizer of microsoft/unixcoder-base, embedded so
  argot's tokenisation matches the reference implementation byte-for-byte.

    https://huggingface.co/microsoft/unixcoder-base
    Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  The model repository ships no NOTICE file (checked 2026-07-29), so
  Apache-2.0 section 4(d) has no upstream notice text to reproduce here.
  argot embeds the tokenizer only — no unixcoder weights and no unixcoder
  code.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored parser — vendor/tree-sitter-pascal/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  A fork of tree-sitter-pascal 0.10.2 with 12 added rules. Its own README
  records what was changed and why; its upstream license travels with the
  vendored directory.


